  "body": "## What\n\nSecond polish pass on the egui shell so it reads like a professional CAM UI\ninstead of a developer build:\n\n- Ribbon group headers (the duplicated, clipped second row) removed; each cell\n  names itself and the row no longer collides.\n- Ribbon cells enlarged (72x40, 24px glyph) with truncated, readable labels.\n- Tab titles capitalised (Browser / Viewport / Properties / Machines).\n- Internal dev status text removed from the status strip.\n- Font tokens bumped for readability (label 13, caption 12.5, row 13.5, ...).\n- Empty viewport shows a one-line hint instead of a bare void.\n- Z=0 ground grid added (1-2-5 steps, zoom-aware, fades at the rim,\n  depth-tested so the part occludes it).\n\n## Done means\n\n- `cargo check` / `cargo clippy -D warnings` / `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`\n  green (442 passed).\n- Release build opens and the ribbon/viewport read cleanly at 2560x1540.\n\n## Changelog\n\nUI: polish ribbon, viewport empty state and ground grid (#N)\nEOF",
